tus per paper is kept in authored/evidence-status.json.","citation_ids":["cite.long.thm-sqrt-bound-route"],"evidence_ids":["mapping.long.thm-sqrt-bound-route"],"id":"long.thm-sqrt-bound-route","kind":"claim","label":"Long record Theorem 6.12 (A square-root bound on the greedy carry)","locator":"Long record Theorem 6.12, p. 48, label thm:sqrt-bound-route","source_id":"paper.long.pdf","statement":"*For the greedy support $G=G_{1/2}$, the centred carry is nonnegative. If in addition\n$$\nC_G(N)\\le2\\sqrt N+4\\qquad\\text{for every }N\\ge0,\n$$\nthen $G$ has infinitely many skipped indices and $X_G(2)=1/2$. The unresolved part is the upper bound along this particular orbit. The carry identity explains its strength: a positive gap $1/2-X_G(2)$ would contribute a term of order $2^N$, which cannot satisfy a square-root bound. This is distinct from the reset-deviation hypothesis of Theorem 6.10; no equivalence between the two hypotheses is asserted.*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/nodes/long.thm-sqrt-bound-route","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/nodes/long.thm-sqrt-bound-route","id":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/edges/%5B%22long.thm-sqrt-bound-route%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.HalfCarryReachability.greedy_half_infinite_of_mobiusCenteredHalfCarry_sqrtBound%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/edges/%5B%22long.thm-sqrt-bound-route%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.HalfCarryReachability.greedy_half_infinite_of_mobiusCenteredHalfCarry_sqrtBound%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","semantic_class":"formalization_correspondence","to":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/nodes/lean.Erdos249257.HalfCarryReachability.greedy_half_infinite_of_mobiusCenteredHalfCarry_s